# A numeric argument making the line longer than a line may be (a
# twentieth of the line's memory: on the vos 209 KB, natively 838 KB):
# the bell, and nothing inserted, where the copy it was built in once
# took memory for good, and on the vos ran out. bash inserts them all,
# so these screens come from our own POSIX build (EDRECORD_SHELL).
rc PS1='$ '
keys ab\e1000000x
snap
keys \e999999y
snap
keys c\r
snap
